{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "02325ceb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Intertidal topography of the Ría de Villaviciosa\n",
    "\n",
    "**A complete worked study with `pyintertidal`** — from raw Sentinel-2 imagery\n",
    "to an elevation model, its ecological interpretation and an independent\n",
    "validation.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is also the reference example of the library. Every step is an\n",
    "explicit function call with its parameters written out in variables, and after\n",
    "each operation a diagram shows what happened to the datacube. Nothing is\n",
    "hidden behind a \"run everything\" call: if you can read this notebook, you know\n",
    "exactly how the result was produced.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Study site.** The Ría de Villaviciosa (Asturias, N Spain) is a mesotidal\n",
    "estuary with sandy flats, a meandering main channel and salt marsh in its\n",
    "upper reaches. It is our reference site: an IGN LiDAR survey covers it, and we\n",
    "have a field transect at Misiego.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What we produce**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Product | What it answers |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Reference map | where the coast is stable and where it is transitional |\n",
    "| Water frequency | how often each pixel is wet |\n",
    "| Intertidal mask | where the intertidal zone is, and how large |\n",
    "| Elevation + uncertainty | how high each pixel stands, and how sure we are |\n",
    "| Sub-pixel relief | where there is structure finer than 10 m |\n",
    "| Hydroperiod & zonation | how long each pixel is submerged → habitat |\n",
    "| Hypsometry | the morphological signature of the estuary |\n",
    "| Validation | how it compares with airborne LiDAR |\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bdd55506",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0 · Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "One import for the library, one connection to Copernicus. The connection is only used if the datacube is not already cached on disk."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "ad216632",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "pyintertidal 0.1.0\n",
      "Authenticated using refresh token.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "import pyintertidal as pit\n",
    "from pyintertidal import SentinelCube, TideService, explain, viz\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"pyintertidal\", pit.__version__)\n",
    "\n",
    "# `connect` also fixes SSL certificate handling on Windows before\n",
    "# authenticating with OpenID Connect (a browser opens the first time).\n",
    "conn = pit.scenes.connect()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "febe4ef1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1 · Study area\n",
    "\n",
    "The area of interest is a **polygon**, not a bounding box. The bounding box is\n",
    "used internally to download a (rectangular) datacube, but every product and\n",
    "every figure is clipped back to the polygon — which is what lets contiguous\n",
    "tiles of a regional campaign fit together without overlaps.\n",
    "\n",
    "The site comes from the registry so the same coordinates are used by this\n",
    "notebook, the validation and the field campaign."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "a37c4bde",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "AOI('Villaviciosa', 44.4 km², [-5.455, 43.470, -5.375, 43.548])\n",
      "  bounding box used for the download: {'west': -5.455, 'south': 43.47, 'east': -5.375, 'north': 43.548}\n",
      "  tide prediction point (centroid):   43.5090, -5.4161\n",
      "  as production tiles of 5 km: 4 cells covering 44.4 km²\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "aoi = pit.sites.get(\"villaviciosa\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(aoi)\n",
    "print(f\"  bounding box used for the download: \"\n",
    "      f\"{ {k: round(v, 3) for k, v in aoi.bbox.items()} }\")\n",
    "print(f\"  tide prediction point (centroid):   \"\n",
    "      f\"{aoi.centroid[0]:.4f}, {aoi.centroid[1]:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# How this AOI would be split for a regional campaign (not used further here):\n",
    "tiles = aoi.tile(cell_km=5)\n",
    "print(f\"  as production tiles of 5 km: {len(tiles)} cells covering \"\n",
    "      f\"{sum(t.area_km2 for t in tiles):.1f} km²\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "aa75d4c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "(<Figure size 1500x1200 with 1 Axes>,\n",
       " <Axes: title={'center': 'Area of interest — Villaviciosa (44.4 km²)'}>)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 3,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1500x1200 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Where the study area actually is. Over satellite imagery, because the first\n",
    "# question about any AOI is whether it covers the estuary you meant and stops\n",
    "# where you meant it to. The outline is the POLYGON, never the bounding box.\n",
    "# `tiles=` overlays the production cells so the regional split can be checked\n",
    "# before launching one notebook per cell.\n",
    "viz.plot_aoi(aoi, tiles=tiles)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8c0eb1cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2 · The datacube\n",
    "\n",
    "All the imagery this study needs is downloaded **once** and cached as a\n",
    "netCDF cube. Every later step streams that file in small time blocks, so\n",
    "memory stays bounded no matter how long the archive is — a decade of imagery\n",
    "over 80 km² would be ≈ 8 GB if loaded whole, and we never load it whole.\n",
    "\n",
    "The bands come from the water detector: NDWI needs B03 and B08 (both native\n",
    "10 m, which is why NDWI has true 10 m resolution), plus SCL for the cloud\n",
    "mask."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "3efb0f37",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[cube] using cache ndwi_cube_villaviciosa_grande_10y.nc\n",
      "1379 scenes · grid 915×915 @ 10 m · EPSG:32630\n",
      "first 2016-01-01 · last 2025-12-29\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Parameters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "TIME_EXTENT   = (\"2016-01-01\", \"2025-12-31\")   # ten years of Sentinel-2\n",
    "WATER         = \"ndwi\"                          # ndwi | mndwi | awei | scl\n",
    "RESOLUTION_M  = 10                              # native for B03/B08\n",
    "CACHE         = \"ndwi_cube_villaviciosa_grande_10y.nc\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Acquisition ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "cube = SentinelCube(aoi, TIME_EXTENT, water=WATER,\n",
    "                    cache_path=CACHE, resolution=RESOLUTION_M)\n",
    "cube.ensure(conn)          # downloads only if the cache does not exist\n",
    "\n",
    "transform, crs = cube.grid\n",
    "print(f\"{len(cube.dates)} scenes · grid {cube.shape[0]}×{cube.shape[1]} \"\n",
    "      f\"@ {abs(transform.a):g} m · {crs}\")\n",
    "print(f\"first {cube.dates[0]} · last {cube.dates[-1]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "rpt-dates",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# What the archive actually offers here. The revisit statistics matter more\n",
    "# than the raw count: a decade with one long gap is not the same archive as a\n",
    "# decade sampled evenly, and those gaps are what later decide which epochs can\n",
    "# be fitted at all. Open \"Every date\" for the full listing.\n",
    "explain.dates_available(cube.dates, TIME_EXTENT)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c0253917",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "What is actually inside that cube — bands as rows, time as columns, filled with real (heavily downsampled) imagery so the clouds and tide states are visible:"
   ]
  },
  {
