    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "explain.summarize(cube)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6d319e45",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We record the rest of the analysis so that, at the end, the notebook can\n",
    "draw the process graph that produced every number in it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "f17a00e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Operation(name='acquire datacube', kind='acquire', params={'water': 'ndwi', 'resolution_m': 10}, inputs=[], outputs=['cube'], before=None, after=None, note='1379 scenes, cached once', seconds=0.0)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 7,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "log = explain.OpLog(\"Villaviciosa 2016–2025\")\n",
    "log.record(\"acquire datacube\", kind=\"acquire\",\n",
    "           params={\"water\": WATER, \"resolution_m\": RESOLUTION_M},\n",
    "           outputs=[\"cube\"],\n",
    "           note=f\"{len(cube.dates)} scenes, cached once\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "95e42d00",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3 · Water detection threshold\n",
    "\n",
    "NDWI separates water from land, but the optimal cut is site-dependent:\n",
    "turbid estuarine water sits lower than the textbook 0.0. Rather than guessing,\n",
    "we let the data decide with Otsu's method over the clearest scenes, and then\n",
    "look at the number before adopting it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "2c68b079",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[water] Otsu on 409,121 clear pixels from 12 scenes → +0.250  (clipped — the sample was not clearly bimodal; set the threshold manually)\n",
      "\n",
      "adopted NDWI threshold: +0.000  (a pixel counts as water when NDWI exceeds this)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Calibration: let the data suggest the threshold ─────────────────────\n",
    "# `calibrate_threshold` ranks the archive by cloudiness, pools the clear-sky\n",
    "# NDWI of the clearest scenes and returns Otsu's split of that sample. A\n",
    "# result pinned at the ends of the allowed range is a warning, not an answer.\n",
    "otsu, info = pit.water.calibrate_threshold(cube, n_scenes=12)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Parameter (adopted explicitly, informed by the calibration) ──────────\n",
    "NDWI_THRESHOLD = 0.0     # turbid estuarine water sits below the textbook 0.1\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(f\"adopted NDWI threshold: {NDWI_THRESHOLD:+.3f}  \"\n",
    "      f\"(a pixel counts as water when NDWI exceeds this)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d9c5c9ad",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4 · Coastal stability and cloud screening\n",
    "\n",
    "Two products from two streaming passes:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Reference map** — each pixel voted wet/dry across the CLEAN scenes and\n",
    "   labelled stable water, stable land or *transition*. The transition class is\n",
    "   the intertidal candidate zone.\n",
    "2. **Per-date cloudiness** — measured globally for clear scenes and, for\n",
    "   cloudy ones, **inside the transition zone only**. That distinction is what\n",
    "   rescues dates: a scene can be 80 % cloudy overall and perfectly clear over\n",
    "   the estuary."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "6fb9580d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  class 0 (transition   ):  116,011 px   11.60 km²\n",
      "  class 1 (stable water ):   24,924 px    2.49 km²\n",
      "  class 2 (stable land  ):  696,290 px   69.63 km²\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Operation(name='reference map + cloud stats', kind='reduce', params={'stable_threshold': 0.95, 'buffer_px': 10}, inputs=['cube'], outputs=['reference map', 'cloud %'], before=None, after=None, note='', seconds=0.0)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 9,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Parameters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "CLEAN_SCENE_MAX_BAD  = 0.05   # a scene votes in the reference map if <5% cloud\n",
    "STABLE_THRESHOLD     = 0.95   # 95% of votes agree → stable water/land\n",
    "TRANSITION_BUFFER_PX = 10     # safety halo around the transition zone\n",
    "BAD_CLASSES          = pit.water.BAD_CLASSES     # SCL cloud/shadow classes\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Reference map + per-date cloudiness ─────────────────────────────────\n",
    "reference_map, cloud_pct = pit.reference_and_clouds(\n",
    "    cube,\n",
    "    threshold=NDWI_THRESHOLD,\n",
    "    bad_classes=BAD_CLASSES,\n",
    "    clean_scene_max_bad=CLEAN_SCENE_MAX_BAD,\n",
    "    stable_threshold=STABLE_THRESHOLD,\n",
    "    transition_buffer_px=TRANSITION_BUFFER_PX,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "px_km2 = abs(transform.a * transform.e) / 1e6\n",
    "for code, name in [(0, \"transition\"), (1, \"stable water\"), (2, \"stable land\")]:\n",
    "    n = int((reference_map == code).sum())\n",
    "    print(f\"  class {code} ({name:13s}): {n:>8,} px  {n * px_km2:6.2f} km²\")\n",
    "\n",
    "log.record(\"reference map + cloud stats\", kind=\"reduce\",\n",
    "           params={\"stable_threshold\": STABLE_THRESHOLD,\n",
    "                   \"buffer_px\": TRANSITION_BUFFER_PX},\n",
    "           inputs=[\"cube\"], outputs=[\"reference map\", \"cloud %\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "90fbf97f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1650x1500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "viz.plot_reference_map(reference_map, transform, crs, aoi);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0487747d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now the date filter. We keep the dates that are clear **over the transition zone**, and measure how many that rescues compared with a whole-scene filter:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "9a865471",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[dates] 1379 acquisitions → 281 clear scenes (20%) → 305 usable after the transition-zone filter (22%)\n",
      "        24 dates recovered (+9% more observations)\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Operation(name='filter dates', kind='filter', params={'cloud_threshold': 0.1}, inputs=[], outputs=['305 dates'], before=None, after=None, note='+9% vs a global filter', seconds=0.0)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 11,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Parameter ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "CLOUD_THRESHOLD = 0.10        # ≤10% cloud over the transition zone\n",
    "\n",
    "usable_dates = pit.filter_dates(cloud_pct, cloud_threshold=CLOUD_THRESHOLD)\n",
    "gain = pit.date_recovery_gain(cloud_pct,\n",
    "                              clean_scene_max_bad=CLEAN_SCENE_MAX_BAD,\n",
    "                              cloud_threshold=CLOUD_THRESHOLD)\n",
    "\n",
    "log.record(\"filter dates\", kind=\"filter\",\n",
    "           params={\"cloud_threshold\": CLOUD_THRESHOLD},\n",
    "           outputs=[f\"{len(usable_dates)} dates\"],\n",
    "           note=f\"+{gain['gain_relative_pct']:.0f}% vs a global filter\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "rpt-clouds",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Which dates survived and, more to the point, WHY. Three outcomes:\n",
    "#   [ref]  clean over the whole scene, so it votes in the reference map\n",
    "#   [✓]    too cloudy globally but clear over the transition zone — an\n",
    "#          observation a whole-scene filter would have thrown away\n",
    "#   [✗]    cloudy where it matters\n",
    "explain.cloud_screening(cloud_pct, usable_dates,\n",
    "                        clean_scene_max_bad=CLEAN_SCENE_MAX_BAD,\n",
    "                        cloud_threshold=CLOUD_THRESHOLD)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "66ef68bc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "What that filter did to the cube — same dimensions, fewer labels:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "e6226199",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
