   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "44cb2d00",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The intertidal zone is the transition class with a water frequency between\n",
    "two bounds. The bounds can be pinned by hand, or found from the data: inside\n",
    "the transition zone the histogram mixes three populations (almost never wet,\n",
    "truly intertidal, almost always wet) and a 3-class Otsu split finds the two\n",
    "valleys between them."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "54a81380",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "multi-Otsu suggests the intertidal window [0.21, 0.66]\n",
      "intertidal zone: 17,822 px = 1.78 km²\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Operation(name='intertidal mask', kind='mask', params={'wf_low': 0.205, 'wf_high': 0.662}, inputs=[], outputs=['intertidal mask'], before=None, after=None, note='1.78 km²', seconds=0.0)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 16,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Parameters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "transition = reference_map == 0\n",
    "WF_LOW, WF_HIGH = pit.multiotsu_window(water_freq, transition)\n",
    "print(f\"multi-Otsu suggests the intertidal window \"\n",
    "      f\"[{WF_LOW:.2f}, {WF_HIGH:.2f}]\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Intertidal mask (also clipped to the study polygon) ─────────────────\n",
    "polygon_mask   = aoi.raster_mask(transform, crs, reference_map.shape)\n",
    "intertidal     = pit.intertidal_mask(water_freq, reference_map,\n",
    "                                     WF_LOW, WF_HIGH, aoi_mask=polygon_mask)\n",
    "\n",
    "area_km2 = intertidal.sum() * px_km2\n",
    "print(f\"intertidal zone: {int(intertidal.sum()):,} px = {area_km2:.2f} km²\")\n",
    "\n",
    "log.record(\"intertidal mask\", kind=\"mask\",\n",
    "           params={\"wf_low\": round(WF_LOW, 3), \"wf_high\": round(WF_HIGH, 3)},\n",
    "           outputs=[\"intertidal mask\"], note=f\"{area_km2:.2f} km²\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "rpt-inter",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Where every pixel of the candidate zone ended up. The transition class is\n",
    "# only a CANDIDATE; the water-frequency window then splits it into ground\n",
    "# almost never wet, ground almost always wet, and the intertidal proper.\n",
    "# Reporting the three together is what makes the window a defensible choice\n",
    "# instead of a magic number — widen it and you see exactly what you gained.\n",
    "explain.intertidal_breakdown(reference_map, water_freq, intertidal,\n",
    "                             WF_LOW, WF_HIGH, transform)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "a93b8c22",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1650x1500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "viz.plot_intertidal(intertidal, transform, crs, aoi,\n",
    "                    title=f\"Intertidal zone · {aoi.name} · {area_km2:.2f} km²\");"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "61f80daf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6 · Tides\n",
    "\n",
    "Elevation methods need the water level at the moment each image was taken, so\n",
    "we pair every usable date with its real acquisition time (from the Copernicus\n",
    "catalogue) and predict the tide there with a global harmonic model.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two refinements worth noting. The prediction point defaults to the polygon\n",
    "centroid, which in a curved estuary can fall on land where the model returns\n",
    "nothing; `water_centroid` instead picks the middle of the main channel. And\n",
    "the continuous series (not the satellite dates) is what later drives the\n",
    "sampling diagnostics and the hydroperiod."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "556def2c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "tide prediction point (mid-channel): 43.5403, -5.3810\n",
      "[tides] model GOT4.10 already cached\n",
      "[tides] GOT4.10 @ (43.540, -5.381) → 305 dates, range [-2.27, 1.21] m\n",
      "reference series: 8,761 hourly predictions, range [-2.35, +2.38] m\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Operation(name='tide heights', kind='apply', params={'model': 'GOT4.10', 'point': '43.540,-5.381'}, inputs=[], outputs=['305 tide heights'], before=None, after=None, note='', seconds=0.0)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 18,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ── Parameters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "TIDE_MODEL = \"GOT4.10\"\n",
    "TIDE_DIR   = \"./tide_models\"\n",
    "\n",
    "tide_point = pit.water_centroid(reference_map, transform, crs)\n",
    "print(f\"tide prediction point (mid-channel): \"\n",
    "      f\"{tide_point[0]:.4f}, {tide_point[1]:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "tides = TideService(model=TIDE_MODEL, directory=TIDE_DIR, location=tide_point)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tide height at each satellite acquisition …\n",
    "tide_heights = tides.heights_for(aoi, usable_dates)\n",
    "\n",
    "# … and the continuous series that represents the real tidal regime.\n",
    "# The full study period, not one year: the tidal frame is a decadal\n",
    "# quantity. The 18.6-year nodal cycle plus the annual and semiannual terms\n",
    "# all move the extremes, so a single year understates the frame our\n",
    "# elevations are referenced to. About a minute of pyTMD for ten years.\n",
    "series_times, series_heights = tides.series(aoi, TIME_EXTENT[0],\n",
    "                                            TIME_EXTENT[1], every_hours=1)\n",
    "print(f\"reference series: {len(series_times):,} hourly predictions, \"\n",
    "      f\"range [{np.nanmin(series_heights):+.2f}, \"\n",
    "      f\"{np.nanmax(series_heights):+.2f}] m\")\n",
    "\n",
    "log.record(\"tide heights\", kind=\"apply\",\n",
    "           params={\"model\": TIDE_MODEL,\n",
    "                   \"point\": f\"{tide_point[0]:.3f},{tide_point[1]:.3f}\"},\n",
    "           outputs=[f\"{len(tide_heights)} tide heights\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e4f4d32c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7 · Is this site mappable?\n",
    "\n",
    "A satellite in a sun-synchronous orbit does not sample the tide evenly, and no\n",
    "elevation method can reconstruct a tide level that was never imaged. These\n",
    "diagnostics put a ceiling on what is achievable here — and belong in the\n",
    "results, not just in the planning."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "a80192ac",
