      "c:\\Users\\Jorge\\sketch_fitton\\Intertidal_analysis\\pyintertidal\\elevation.py:411: RuntimeWarning: All-NaN slice encountered\n",
      "  f\"{np.nanmedian(self.sigma_mu[v]) * 100:.1f} cm\")\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dem_step = pit.fit_step(\n",
    "    cube, tide_heights, dates=latest[\"dates\"],\n",
    "    threshold=NDWI_THRESHOLD, min_obs=5,\n",
    "    clip_mask=intertidal, epoch_label=latest[\"label\"],\n",
    ")\n",
    "dem_step.summary()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\ncoverage: HSR {int(np.isfinite(dem.mu).sum()):,} px vs \"\n",
    "      f\"step {int(np.isfinite(dem_step.mu).sum()):,} px\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7395219",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9 · Validation against airborne LiDAR\n",
    "\n",
    "The IGN 5 m LiDAR survey is an independent measurement of the same surface.\n",
    "Two cautions before reading the numbers, and the second is the important one.\n",
    "\n",
    "Our elevations are referenced to the tide-model datum and LiDAR to an\n",
    "orthometric one, so their offset appears as a **bias** that says nothing about\n",
    "method skill. RMSE and MAE are therefore computed after removing it.\n",
    "\n",
    "**This reference is not adequate for the intertidal zone.** The INSPIRE WCS\n",
    "serves the product as `int16`, i.e. rounded to the metre — across our whole\n",
    "intertidal range there are seven distinct values, and that rounding alone\n",
    "contributes 1/√12 = 0.29 m of RMSE. Worse, the survey flies at whatever tide\n",
    "state it finds, so over a flooded flat it returns the water surface rather\n",
    "than the bed. The next cell quantifies exactly that, and any ranking of\n",
    "methods built on these numbers should be treated as uninformative until a\n",
    "float-precision reference (MDT05 from the download centre, or the field\n",
    "transect) is available."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d5549b77",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "LiDAR reprojected onto the analysis grid: 100% coverage\n"
     ]
    },
    {
