  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "be44e37a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### The check that needs no elevation model at all\n",
    "\n",
    "Water frequency must be **negatively** correlated with elevation: higher\n",
    "ground floods less often. That is close to model-free — it only counts how\n",
    "often each pixel was wet — which makes it the right arbiter when the\n",
    "reference DEM itself is in doubt.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run it on every elevation raster in play, including the LiDAR. Whichever\n",
    "raster fails this test is the one to distrust."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "546ed4e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "{'spearman': -0.1581, 'pearson': -0.1792, 'n': 17822}"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 25,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "pit.validation.wf_vs_elevation(water_freq, lidar, mask=intertidal)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b9d5b647",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Field transect — Misiego\n",
    "\n",
    "The profile we survey on the ground, with both satellite methods and the LiDAR\n",
    "plotted against it. Bring this figure to the field: the x axis is metres walked\n",
    "from the start point."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8a598ee9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# The line must CROSS the flat, which the previous coordinates did not: they\n",
    "# ran up a hillside to 46 m and returned zero intertidal pixels. These were\n",
    "# chosen by searching for the trace with the most intertidal coverage and the\n",
    "# largest drop — check them against the real Misiego site before walking it.\n",
    "TRANSECT_START = (-5.3914, 43.5168)     # (lon, lat)\n",
    "TRANSECT_END   = (-5.3914, 43.5140)     # 310 m, 90 % inside the mask\n",
    "\n",
    "profiles = {}\n",
    "for label, raster in [(\"HSR\", dem.mu), (\"step (DEA)\", dem_step.mu),\n",
    "                      (\"IGN LiDAR\", lidar)]:\n",
    "    distance, values = pit.transect_profile(raster, transform, crs,\n",
    "                                            TRANSECT_START, TRANSECT_END, n=200)\n",
    "    profiles[label] = values\n",
    "\n",
    "# `start`/`end` plus a raster draw the trace on a map beside the profile —\n",
    "# the panel that catches a transect placed somewhere it was not meant to go.\n",
    "viz.plot_transect(distance, profiles, title=\"Misiego transect · profiles\",\n",
    "                  start=TRANSECT_START, end=TRANSECT_END,\n",
    "                  basemap_of=dem.mu, transform=transform, crs=crs, aoi=aoi);"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1f3fe855",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10 · From topography to habitat\n",
    "\n",
    "Elevation is a means, not an end. What organises intertidal life is the\n",
    "**hydroperiod**: the fraction of time a spot is submerged. Computing it from\n",
    "the continuous tide series (not from the satellite dates, which are unevenly\n",
    "sampled) turns our DEM into an ecological map."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f2211a74",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "hydroperiod: 17% – 99% of the time submerged (median 44%)\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    },
    {
