  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e0040298",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Morphological signature\n",
    "\n",
    "The hypsometric curve — how much area lies below each elevation — is the\n",
    "compact fingerprint of the estuary's shape, and the natural quantity to\n",
    "compare between epochs or between sites."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "04d9bf14",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[hypsometry] Villaviciosa\n",
      "  intertidal area   1.72 km²\n",
      "  elevation range   -2.06 … +1.02 m (median +0.24)\n",
      "  hypsometric integral 0.698 → convex — area concentrated high (accretional signature)\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 700x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "curve = pit.hypsometry.hypsometric_curve(dem.mu, transform)\n",
    "summary = pit.hypsometry.describe(curve, aoi.name)\n",
    "\n",
    "pit.hypsometry.plot_curves({aoi.name: curve},\n",
    "                           title=f\"Hypsometric curve · {aoi.name}\");"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "83079ba0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Change between epochs\n",
    "\n",
    "With two epochs fitted, the difference is a change map. The rule that keeps it\n",
    "honest: **never subtract two DEMs without their uncertainties**. Only changes\n",
    "larger than the propagated uncertainty are reported."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "150d82af",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "comparing 2020-2022 → 2023-2025\n",
      "[morphodynamics] 2020-2022 → 2023-2025\n",
      "  11,839 of 15,996 pixels changed significantly (74%) at 1.96σ\n",
      "  accretion +30,249 m³ over 0.13 km²\n",
      "  erosion   -235,462 m³ over 1.05 km²\n",
      "  net       -205,213 m³ → eroding\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1650x1500 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "if len(epoch_list) >= 2:\n",
    "    previous = epoch_list[-2]\n",
    "    print(f\"comparing {previous['label']} → {latest['label']}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    dem_prev = pit.fit_hsr(cube, tide_heights, dates=previous[\"dates\"],\n",
    "                           scale=SCALE, max_uncertainty=MAX_UNCERTAINTY,\n",
    "                           clip_mask=intertidal, epoch_label=previous[\"label\"],\n",
    "                           superresolve=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "    change = pit.morphodynamics.dem_difference(\n",
    "        dem_prev.mu, dem.mu, dem_prev.sigma_mu, dem.sigma_mu, confidence=1.96)\n",
    "    budget = pit.morphodynamics.summarize(change, transform,\n",
    "                                          f\"{previous['label']} → {latest['label']}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    viz.plot_map(np.where(change[\"significant\"], change[\"change\"], np.nan),\n",
    "                 transform, crs, aoi, cmap=\"RdBu_r\", vmin=-0.3, vmax=0.3,\n",
    "                 robust=False, title=\"Significant elevation change\",\n",
    "                 cbar_label=\"Δ elevation (m)\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"only one epoch available — skip the change analysis\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cb942afe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
