  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b4da65ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Finally, write the products, package them with STAC metadata that carries the parameters, and build a single self-contained HTML report."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "873996fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[export] STAC collection with 1 items → products_villaviciosa\\collection.json\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "('products_villaviciosa\\\\collection.json',\n",
       " ['products_villaviciosa\\\\hsr_elevation.json'])"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 33,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "OUT_DIR = \"products_villaviciosa\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Rasters (10 m grid, clipped to the polygon) + the super-resolved DEM\n",
    "dem.save(OUT_DIR)\n",
    "pit.write_geotiff(f\"{OUT_DIR}/water_frequency.tif\", water_freq,\n",
    "                  transform, crs, \"float32\", np.nan)\n",
    "pit.write_geotiff(f\"{OUT_DIR}/intertidal_mask.tif\",\n",
    "                  intertidal.astype(\"uint8\"), transform, crs, \"uint8\", None)\n",
    "pit.write_geotiff(f\"{OUT_DIR}/hydroperiod.tif\", hydro,\n",
    "                  transform, crs, \"float32\", np.nan)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Provenance travels with the data\n",
    "item = pit.export.stac_item(\n",
    "    f\"{OUT_DIR}/hsr_elevation.tif\", aoi=aoi,\n",
    "    datetime_utc=f\"{latest['label'][-4:]}-07-01\",\n",
    "    properties={\"pyintertidal:method\": \"hsr\",\n",
    "                \"pyintertidal:epoch\": latest[\"label\"],\n",
    "                \"pyintertidal:ndwi_threshold\": NDWI_THRESHOLD,\n",
    "                \"pyintertidal:cloud_threshold\": CLOUD_THRESHOLD,\n",
    "                \"pyintertidal:wf_window\": [round(WF_LOW, 3), round(WF_HIGH, 3)],\n",
    "                \"pyintertidal:min_obs\": MIN_OBS,\n",
    "                \"pyintertidal:tide_model\": TIDE_MODEL},\n",
    "    assets={\"uncertainty\": f\"{OUT_DIR}/hsr_uncertainty.tif\",\n",
    "            \"subpixel_relief\": f\"{OUT_DIR}/hsr_sigma.tif\"})\n",
    "pit.export.write_stac([item], OUT_DIR,\n",
    "                      description=f\"Intertidal products · {aoi.name}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "46669a31",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "report written to products_villaviciosa/report_villaviciosa.html\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "report_path = pit.report.site_report(\n",
    "    f\"{OUT_DIR}/report_villaviciosa.html\",\n",
    "    aoi, cube=cube,\n",
    "    params={\"period\": f\"{TIME_EXTENT[0]} → {TIME_EXTENT[1]}\",\n",
    "            \"water detector\": WATER, \"NDWI threshold\": NDWI_THRESHOLD,\n",
    "            \"cloud threshold\": CLOUD_THRESHOLD, \"min observations\": MIN_OBS,\n",
    "            \"intertidal window\": f\"[{WF_LOW:.2f}, {WF_HIGH:.2f}]\",\n",
    "            \"epoch\": latest[\"label\"], \"tide model\": TIDE_MODEL},\n",
    "    coverage=metrics, verdict=verdict,\n",
    "    validation=rows, zones=zone_table, oplog=log,\n",
    "    notes=\"Satellite-derived intertidal topography, produced with pyintertidal.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"report written to\", report_path)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3f9b9ca1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Scaling out.** To map another area, change the polygon in section 1 —\n",
    "  nothing else. Each tile caches its own cube and can run in a separate\n",
    "  process; :mod:`pyintertidal.mosaic` merges the results and checks the seams.\n",
    "* **Method comparison.** The superseded elevation methods (bracketing,\n",
    "  waterline isolines, and the server-side variants) remain runnable in\n",
    "  `pyintertidal.legacy`, which is what the paper's comparison section uses.\n",
    "* **Reproducibility.** Every parameter in this notebook is a named variable,\n",
    "  and the same values are stored in the STAC item and the HTML report, so a\n",
    "  result found later can always be traced back to the run that made it.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
